Section 127. The Employee Welfare Fund shall consist of:
  (1) Contributions and Supplementary Contributions;
  (2) money belonging to the Employee Welfare Fund under Section 133
and Section 136;
  (3) additional money under Section 131;
  (4) fnes received from the punishment of offenders under this Act;
  (5) donated money or properties;
  (6) subsidies paid by the Government;
  (7) other income; and
  (8) interest or fruit of the Employee Welfare Fund.
 The Employee Welfare Fund shall arrange the following accounts:
  (1) an account of each member stating Contributions, Supplementary
Contributions and fruit produced by such money; and
  (2) a central account stating particulars of other money besides that
in (1). Section 128. A fne which is remitted under Section 127(4) into the Employee Welfare
Fund and the due of remittance of such money shall be made under the rules prescribed by
the Employee Welfare Fund Committee which are published in the Government Gazette.
